suspend/resume cycle leaves the directory identical to its pre-suspend state.
Activity inference works from =AI-WorkPlan.org= dblock header when the symlink
is absent (which it is after suspend). Added both to =examples= output.

* DONE [#B] <<Skills Directory Layout>> Design directory layout for skills :ai:
CLOSED: [2026-07-13 Sun] SCHEDULED: <2026-07-13 Sun>
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:07
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 5 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
Decide the on-disk layout for skills under templates:
- =mother/_skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md= for baseline skills
- =<activity>/_skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md= for activity-specific skills
- Should activity skills override mother skills of the same name, or
  should both be installed side-by-side under =.claude/skills/=?
Document the resolution rule in =AI-Activity.org= (mother) once decided.
----- AI Results: ------
Chose the activity-root layout =<activity>/_skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md=,
NOT nested under =_claude/=. Rationale: skills are semantically distinct
from =.claude/= machinery (settings, commands) — they're documentation /
knowledge. Placing them at the activity root keeps them independently
visible to humans and other tools; the installed location under
=.claude/skills/= is just where Claude Code looks. Resolution rule
mirrors =_claude/= entries: activity =_skills/= if present, else fall
back to =mother/_skills/=. Activity replaces mother wholesale (no
side-by-side merging) — same semantics as the existing =_claude/=
handling.

