* DONE [#A] <<Provenance Line>> Multi-line org-comment provenance in safe-copied files :ai:
CLOSED: [2026-07-16 Tue] SCHEDULED: <2026-07-16 Tue>
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:11
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 10 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
After the safe-copy of =AI-DevStatus.org= and =AI-WorkPlan.org= (and
before dblock expansion), insert a multi-line org-comment block
recording: date (ISO 8601 with tz), user (=USER= env → =LOGNAME= env
→ =os.getlogin()= → =pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid())=), templates base
(actually used, via =_resolveTemplatesBase=), and =sys.argv=. Placement:
after the last =#+= directive at the top of the file. Not a dblock
--- inert text, written once at install time, never regenerated.
Rationale: elisp dblock expanders can't recover invocation context;
provenance must be birth-certificate data.
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented in =py3/bin/aiActivity.cs=. New helpers
=_detectUser()= (4-tier fallback chain, handles nohup/detached shells
where =os.getlogin()= raises) and =_writeProvenanceLine()= (scans for
last =#+= header, inserts multi-line comment block). Called from
both =initiate= and =initiateSub= safe-copy sites. Verified in test
runs --- provenance appears at the top of both editable files with
correct date, user (=bystar=), templates path, and full command line.
=aiSuspend= / =aiResume= treat provenance as opaque file content, so
it survives suspend/resume cycles unchanged.

* DONE [#A] <<noLink Override>> --noLink CLI flag for safe-copy override :ai:
CLOSED: [2026-07-16 Tue] SCHEDULED: <2026-07-16 Tue>
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:11
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 10 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
Add =--noLink=<filename>= parameter to both =initiate= and =initiateSub=.
When passed, the named file is safe-copied instead of being installed
as a symlink. Applies to =CLAUDE.md=, =AI-WORKFLOW.org=, and
=AI-Activity.org= (files the engine would otherwise install as
symlinks). Not applicable to =.claude/= entries. Single filename only
for now; multi-file support later via a =bisos.b= framework improvement
(=nargs='+'= or =append= action on =parDictAdd=).
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented. Chose CLI-flag over per-activity config file after
discussion --- preserves the principle that templates should stay
passive (a filesystem of examples, not a configuration layer). Two
new =parDictAdd= entries (=noLink= in the =commonParamsSpecify=
common list), classHead dblocks for both =initiate= and =initiateSub=
extended with =noLink= in =parsOpt=, and the symlink-installation
sites in both commands now branch on =noLink == fname= to select
=shutil.copy2()= vs =symlink_to()=. Log messages distinguish the
two behaviors (=SYMLINKED:= vs =COPIED (--noLink=<file>):=). All four
combinations tested (default, =--noLink=AI-Activity.org=,
=--noLink=CLAUDE.md=, =initiateSub --noLink=AI-Activity.org=).
=verify.sh= regression-clean.

