* DONE [#A] Add to documentation the concept of "Homogenous and Heterogeneous AI-Activities" :aiAndMe:
CLOSED: [2026-07-27 Sun]
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:12
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 12 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
SCHEDULED: <2026-07-27 Mon 11:56>
When all the directories and the repo of those directories all have references to a single set of
ai-templates, we call that Homogenous AI-Activities. Example is that of a group of collaborators
using one set of templates base for python convention pip package development and latex conventions for documentation.
------
When some  directories in the repo have references to different sets of ai-templates, we call that Heterogeneous
AI-Activities. An example would be when you are developing some proprietary pip packages with one set of ai-templates
and open-source pip packages with a different set of ai-templates.
-----
aiActivity.cs supports both.
Add this to the README.org
----- AI Results: ------
Added new "AI-Activity Topology" section to =README.org= under Usage, covering
both dimensions in two subsections (Homogeneous/Heterogeneous and
Hierarchical/Lateral) with concrete examples. TOC entry added. Notes that the two
axes are orthogonal and combinable, and that =--templates= / the forthcoming
per-directory override are the mechanisms for Heterogeneous topologies.

* DONE [#A] Add to documentation the concept of "Lateral AI-Activities and Hierarchical AI-Activities" :aiAndMe:
CLOSED: [2026-07-27 Sun]
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:12
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 12 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
SCHEDULED: <2026-07-27 Mon 11:56>
When working on a project, you may be working on a set of directories that fall under the same repo.
We call that Hierarchical AI-Activities. In one directory you do pip pkg dev. And under it you do its latex doc.
This would be called Hierarchical AI-Activities
-----
Work on a project may involve visiting multiple repos. This would be called a Laterial AI-Activity.
----
aiActivity.cs supports both.
Homogenous and Heterogenous and Lateral and Hierarchical can be combined.
Add this to the README.org
----- AI Results: ------
Covered in the same "AI-Activity Topology" section as TODO 1 above (combined as
planned). Hierarchical = nested dirs / =initiate= + =initiateSub=; Lateral =
multiple independent repos each =initiate=-d, Claude walk-up picks up both.
Noted that all four variants combine freely.

