* DONE [#A] <<Add a .aiActivity.cs to the current directory>> that captures and defines templates directory :aiAndMe:
CLOSED: [2026-07-27 Sun]
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-22 Tue 22:12
:ARCHIVE_FILE: /bxRepos/bisos-pip/aiActivity/AI-WorkPlan.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Stage 12 TODOs
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: AI-WorkPlan
:ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
:END:
SCHEDULED: <2026-07-21 Tue 13:41>
In the case of Heterogenous AI-Activities, one needs to change the templates parameter for aiActivity.cs.
In situations when one works with different template dirs it is possible to confuse re-creations and resumes.
Existence of a .aiActivity.cs/fps/templates in the current directory over rides the value in
~/.config/bisos/aiActivity.cs/fps/templates
This makes usafge more  convenient. Also upon creation of the repo this can be configured to move towards less config.
----- AI Results: ------
Implemented as a separate CSU rather than a =--cwd= flag on =userConfig_csu=.
Initial implementation added =--cwd= to =userConfig_csu.parGet/parSet= and
its two commands; the user reviewed and pushed back --- correctly --- that
composition-of-CSUs is the better factoring. Redone as follows:

- New module =bisos.b.cwdConfig_csu= (source + venv). Mirrors
  =userConfig_csu= structurally but its =_configRoot()= returns
  =<cwd>/.<csxu-name>/fps/= (hidden dotdir) instead of the =~/.config/=
  path. Exposes =cwdConfig_get= and =cwdConfig_set= commands with the
  same =--parName= / =--parValue= interface. Reuses the =parName= /
  =parValue= params declared by =userConfig_csu= (its own
  =commonParamsSpecify()= is empty).
- =userConfig_csu= reverted to its pre-Stage-12 shape --- no =cwd=
  parameter anywhere. No LSP diagnostics remain.
- =aiActivity.cs= adds =bisos.b.cwdConfig_csu= to its csuList
  alongside =bisos.b.userConfig_csu= (both the elisp block and the
  =csuList= list). Imports both modules. The =examples= command
  invokes =cwdConfig_csu.examples_csu().pyCmnd()= right after the
  =userConfig_csu= one, so the top-level =examples= menu shows both
  =userConfig_get/set= and =cwdConfig_get/set= chapters.
- =_resolveTemplatesBase()= composes them: step 2 is
  =cwdConfig_csu.parGet('templates')=, step 3 is
  =userConfig_csu.parGet('templates')=. Each reads only its own
  store; the precedence policy lives here, not in the CSUs.
- End-to-end smoke test verified: =cwdConfig_set --parName=templates=
  writes to =./.aiActivity.cs/fps/templates/value=; =cwdConfig_get=
  reads it back; unset case reports =(not set)=; examples menu shows
  both CSUs' chapters as expected.


