----- AI Results: ------

*First cut (2026-10-07); accepted the same day after the revisions below.*

*Location (decided in discussion):* not here, but in the templates repo
(=bisos/defaults=), next to the commands it depicts. Path:
=ai-templates/_nonTemplate_/images/aiWorkflow-graphviz.pcs= (+ png, pdf, svg,
jpg, gv, title, caption).
- =_nonTemplate_/= is the templates tree's /one/ escape from the templates
  concept. Everything in a templates repo is a template or relates to one;
  material about the tree itself (images, docs, ...) goes under this single
  directory as subdirectories.
- A general "=_=-prefix = not an activity" pattern was considered and
  rejected. One explicit escape is enough by construction, and a pattern
  would silently hide any =_foo/= someone creates.
- =bxexamples= receives the figure by the Stage 15 sync, not by authoring
  there. This repo's README can later link to it by its bxexamples GitHub URL.

*Engine change (=aiActivity.cs=):* new module-level
=nonActivityDirs = {'mother', 'test', '_nonTemplate_'}=, replacing the
=examples=-only =excludedDirs=. It is now also enforced as a refusal in
=initiate=, =initiateSub= and =aiResume=: =--activity=mother= /
=--activity=_nonTemplate_= give
=Not an activity: ... (reserved: _nonTemplate_, mother, test)= and create
no files. Before this, any existing directory, including =mother=, was
accepted. Verified in a scratch dir; =examples= no longer lists
=_nonTemplate_=.

*Figure decisions*:
- Layers top to bottom, labelled in a left column: Setup (once per
  directory) → Session start → Work loop (per TODO) → Session end.
- mid-layer3 uses =/bx-commit-msg=. The spec said =/bx-ai-outputs= for
  the commit message, which reads as a slip.
- Fill = effect on files:
  - blue = /read/ (loads into the session, changes no files)
  - pink = /write/ (records session knowledge into files)
  - purple = /read-write/
  Mnemonic: blue + pink = purple.
- The classification: read = =/bx-confirm0=, =/bx-confirm-here=,
  =/bx-status=, =/bx-import-archive=. write = =/bx-done=,
  =/bx-update-status=. read-write = =/bx-initiate=, the work itself,
  =/bx-commit-msg=, =/bx-ai-outputs= (index reads, capture writes),
  =/bx-archive=, =/bx-context-trim=.
- Solid border = always, dashed = perhaps. "Perhaps" steps sit inline on
  the main path rather than with skip-edges. A dashed node means "may be
  skipped", which keeps the figure clean.
- Additions beyond the spec:
  - =/bx-status= as a perhaps-alternative at session start
  - =/bx-context-trim= in the session-end layer ([[16.4]])
  - =/bx-initiate= marked perhaps, with "(or aiActivity.cs -i initiate
    from the shell)"
- The =next TODO= loop runs from =/bx-done= back to =/bx-import-archive=
  (green, =constraint=false=). =end of session= exits to
  =/bx-update-status=.
- The legend is an HTML table inside the figure.

*Pointer:* one line added to =mother/AI-WORKFLOW.org= under the
slash-commands table:
=[[file:../_nonTemplate_/images/aiWorkflow.png]]=. As discussed, the link
works on GitHub and when the real file is opened, but not through a
project's symlink in Emacs unless =find-file-visit-truename= is set.

*Rendering:* uses the same =PYTHONPATH= workaround as [[12.2]] (old
=bisos.graphviz= 0.29 in the bisos3 venv).

*Commits:* two repos.
- =bisos/defaults=: =_nonTemplate_/= (new), =mother/AI-WORKFLOW.org=
- this repo: =py3/bin/aiActivity.cs=, =AI-WorkPlan.org=

*Second cut (same day): scope narrowed and write targets added.*
- *Scope = usage of an existing setup.* =/bx-initiate= and
  =/bx-context-trim= removed, and with them the Setup layer. Both shape the
  setup and belong to a separate figure about how the templates and setup
  are created. The figure now starts at Session start.
- *Write targets.* A column of five subjects on the right, each on the rank
  of its main writer:
  - =Repo content (working tree)= ← Work
  - =Repo git (.git)= ← =/bx-commit-msg=, labelled
    =.git/CLAUDE_COMMIT_MSG / you commit=. Splitting git from content makes
    the "Claude writes the message, you commit" boundary visible.
  - =AI-Outputs.org (cross-project)=, grey as in the structure figure ←
    =/bx-ai-outputs= (capture)
  - =AI-WorkPlan.org (+ _archive)= ← =/bx-done=, =/bx-archive=. The archive
    file is folded in rather than drawn as a separate subject.
  - =AI-DevStatus.org= ← =/bx-update-status=
- *Writes only*, as red arrows. Reads stay encoded in the fill colour.
  Drawing reads too would roughly triple the edges. The full read/write
  matrix (command × subject) was worked out in discussion. It is a
  candidate for a table in =AI-WORKFLOW.org= next to the figure.
- *What the figure now shows:* only "Work" touches repo content. Every
  =/bx-*= command manages AI state (WorkPlan, DevStatus, Outputs) or, for
  =/bx-commit-msg=, only a message file in =.git=.
- *Layout:*
  - =group= attributes plus an invisible chain keep the main path and the
    subject column straight
  - the dotted =update-status — archive= link was dropped; the shared rank
    already shows they go together
  - west ports on the =next TODO= loop were tried and reverted, because dot
    then crossed the main path twice
- Legend gains =red arrow = writes=. =AI-WORKFLOW.org= pointer text updated.

*Third cut (same day): renamed, locality, your git write, table.*
- *Renamed* =aiWorkflow= → =aiUsageWorkflow= (the =.pcs=, the graph name,
  all outputs). The old outputs were removed. A sibling
  =aiStartupWorkflow= figure is planned for setup/templates creation;
  Mohsen wrote =uiStartupWorkflow=, read as a typo. Paths above that say
  =aiWorkflow= are historical.
- *Locality by position.* =AI-Outputs.org= moved to the /left/ of the main
  path, which is outside this repo and shared across projects. The right
  column is now purely this repo. The legend's second row says so.
- *Repo content → Repo git* as a dashed black arrow labelled
  =you: git add, git commit -t=: a write by /you/, not Claude. The
  commit-msg node lost its "git add, then" prefix and its edge label is
  now just =.git/CLAUDE_COMMIT_MSG=. Legend: "red arrow = Claude writes",
  "dashed black arrow = you write".
- *Read/write table* captured as
  =_nonTemplate_/images/aiUsageWorkflow.org=, which also holds the figure
  link, the full R/W matrix (including a /You/ row and the index vs
  capture modes of =/bx-ai-outputs=), notes on reading it, and the fill
  colour key. =AI-WORKFLOW.org= now points to both the PNG and this
  table.
- *Graphviz lessons* (worth adding to the graphviz-authoring skill):
  - Source order within a =rank=same= subgraph is /not/ honoured. Neither
    =dir='back'= nor a labelled flat edge pinned the order. What works is
    invisible flat edges (=label → left node → spine=), which dot always
    draws left to right.
  - A long back-edge (the =next TODO= loop) can't be steered by ports.
    Route it through invisible point waypoints, one per rank, chained top
    to bottom with =dir='back'= on the first segment and =dir='none'= on
    the rest, so it doesn't fight the ranking. Zero-size points leave
    gaps in the line; use =width=0.03= in the edge colour.

