Show the aiActivity.cs -i commands for initiate, the template files in the
templates dir, and /bx-context-trim. Scope: creating and shaping a setup;
[[14.2]] (aiUsageWorkflow) covers using one.
----- Results: ------

*First cut (2026-10-07); accepted the same day after the revisions below.*
=_nonTemplate_/images/aiStartupWorkflow-graphviz.pcs= + all outputs.
- *Same visual language as =aiUsageWorkflow=*: stage labels on the left,
  a straight main path, left of the main path = shared (outside this repo,
  grey), right = this repo. Same fills (read/write/read-write) and borders
  (always/perhaps).
- *Stages:*
  1. Discover: =aiActivity.cs= examples menu
  2. Install: =-i initiate= / =-i initiateSub= / =--noLink= /
     =/bx-initiate=
  3. Inspect: =listClaudesPath=, =startupClaudeTokens=
  4. Trim: =/bx-context-trim=
  5. Use: a hand-off node to =aiUsageWorkflow=
  6. Maintain: =refresh=, =aiSuspend= / =aiResume=, =deClaudify=
- *Subjects:*
  - Left: =mother/= and =<activity>/= with their template files.
  - Right: Symlinks (→ templates) and Safe-copies (yours).
  - cwdConfig was dropped as an auto-persist detail already in the
    structure figure.
- *Writers:* a new colour for =aiActivity.cs= writes (green, matching the
  engine node in the structure figure; dashed = symlink, solid = copy),
  alongside red = Claude. Grey hollow arrows mark the templates as source.
- *=/bx-context-trim=* writes in both directions on its own row: a /shared
  edit (confirmed separately)/ to =<activity>/AI-Activity.org + its
  imports= on the left, and /local trims/ to WorkPlan/DevStatus (via
  =/bx-archive=, =/bx-update-status=) on the right. That is the
  local/shared distinction the command enforces.
- *Loop*: =chain grew= from Usage back to Inspect, through left
  waypoints.
- *Layout lesson:* the first render drew Trim and Maintain writes as long
  back-edges to subjects at the top, and they tangled. Fixed with
  /reference nodes/: each later stage gets thin-bordered nodes on its own
  rank that stand for a subject drawn above. Every write edge is then
  short. The legend explains the thin border.
- =mother/AI-WORKFLOW.org=: pointer added in "How These Files Are Set Up".

