Import it in aiActivity.cs and use it and see how useful it is.
----- Results: ------

Written as =py3/bisos/aiActivity/startupClaudeTokens_csu.py= (name per [[16.1]]),
a rewrite rather than a port of the outline. Wired into =aiActivity.cs=:
added to the elisp =csuList= block and the =csuListProc= body, and its
=examples_csu()= is called after =listClaudesPath= in =examples=.
- *NOTE:* =py-dblock.cs= has no =csuListProc= handler, so the generated
  body was hand-edited to match the generator's output. Regenerate in Blee
  to confirm.

Usage: =aiActivity.cs -i startupClaudeTokens= (no params; operates on cwd;
read-only). The output has these sections, in Claude Code's load order:
- managed policy
- user =~/.claude=
- walk-up chain (=/= → cwd) with the =@=-import tree indented by hop
- auto-memory =MEMORY.md=
- skill + command descriptions
- on-demand files (=CLAUDE.md= overlays below cwd, path-scoped rules,
  =AI-Outputs.org=), listed but not summed into the startup total
- heaviest-5 with percentage share, then the startup total

=opResults= is a dict (=startupTokens=, =onDemandTokens=, =bySection=).
Shared files are counted once; repeats are shown as =already loaded=.

Tested (2026-10-07):
- repo root: ~76K tokens at startup, ~13K on demand
- =py3/tests/=: ~78K
- an empty dir: 0
- parser checks: email addresses, code spans, fenced blocks and escaped
  spaces handled correctly

*How useful --- first findings from this repo:*
- ~74K of the ~76K comes from the walk-up chain, and ~59K of that is
  =bisos-pip/AI-Activity.org='s 12 =@= imports. Only ~4.5K is the file
  itself. The three heaviest are the terminology panel (~9K),
  =bxGenesis/start/README.org= (~7.7K, CI/CD pointer) and the bisos-pip
  panel list (~7.6K). These are candidates for "mention, don't import"
  (drop the =@=; Claude Code skips only /markdown/ code spans, so org
  markup is not a reliable way to suppress an import) or moving into a
  skill.
- =AI-DevStatus.org= is ~8.5K, the second-heaviest item. It is worth
  trimming at the next =/bx-update-status=.
- Skill + command descriptions cost only ~2K for 26 entries. Skills are
  cheap at startup, which supports moving content out of
  =AI-Activity.org= into skills.
- *It found a real defect:* =py3/tests/CLAUDE.md= is still a *legacy
  symlink* (pre-Stage-11). Its =@./AI-Activity.org= etc. resolve into
  =mother/=, the exact Stage 11 bug. The tool flags this with
  =!! resolved via symlink into ...=. Fix: =aiActivity.cs -i refresh=
  in =py3/tests/=.

=aiStatusOutine.py= is superseded but left in place (untracked). Delete
when convenient.

Follow-up (same day, Mohsen's request): skill/command lines used to name
only the =.claude= dir, which hid that =.claude/skills= and
=.claude/commands= are symlinks into the templates tree. Each directory
now gets a header line that shows its symlink target and subtotal, e.g.
=.claude/skills -> .../ai-templates/bisos-pip/_skills=, with its entries
indented below. That makes it visible which templates tree and activity
supplied them. Headers are excluded from the section total and from the
heaviest-5 list.

