Describe how it fits in the overall workflow.
- Also add a README section on Claude specificity: the AI-*.org files are
  the agent-neutral payload; =CLAUDE.md= + =.claude/= (+ =startupClaudeTokens=,
  =listClaudesPath=, =deClaudify=) are the /Claude binding/. Say plainly that
  only the Claude binding exists today, and what a second binding would need
  (an entry file the agent loads, walk-up, and =@= imports or a generated
  concatenation). See the design decision in =AI-DevStatus.org=.
----- Results: ------

=README.org= changes:
- *New top-level section* "Claude Specificity: Agent-Neutral Content, Claude
  Binding", placed after "Two-Part Architecture". It covers:
  - the agent-neutral content and engine logic vs the Claude binding
  - the three Claude Code behaviors the design relies on
  - that only the Claude binding exists today
  - what a second binding would need: an entry file, walk-up, imports.
    Imports are the real dependency, since concatenation would give up
    shared-template propagation.
  - the "isolate, not abstract" policy
  A one-line pointer to it was added at the end of "Two-Part Architecture".
- *Usage → Table of Commands*: new "Inspection commands" group.
  =listClaudesPath= moved there from the lifecycle table, and
  =startupClaudeTokens= added.
- *New Usage subsection* "Inspect the Startup Context:
  =startupClaudeTokens=". It covers:
  - what the command reports, in Claude Code's load order
  - startup vs on-demand
  - an abridged real output excerpt from this repo
  - how to read it (59K of 76K is =AI-Activity.org='s imports)
  - remedies: mention instead of import, move to a skill, archive
  - the symlink-resolution diagnostic
  - where it fits in the workflow
  - that counts are estimates
- *Key Files*: added =startupClaudeTokens_csu.py=, and corrected the stale
  command list for =aiActivity.cs=.
- *TOC* entries added by hand; toc-org will regenerate them on the next
  save in Emacs.

Two corrections made while writing:
- "Wrap in backticks" is not a valid way to mention without importing in
  org files (Claude Code skips only markdown code spans). The README says
  "drop the =@=", and the 16.2 results are fixed to match.
- Starting a session inside an =initiateSub= overlay does not reduce
  startup tokens, because the ancestors still load. The README says so
  explicitly.

The figure is not done here. It belongs with the =py3/images= TODOs
(12.2, 14.2).
